In chemistry, acid mixed with base creates a salt; eg
HCl + NaOH = H2O + NaCL  (salt and water)

Thusly, if we mix a salt with an acid, a base will result. The base 
which is created is dependent upon the acid used, assuming the salt is 
standard table salt NaCl. Is a potion of acid hydrocloric (HCl), 
sulfuric (H2SO4), phosphoric acid (H3PO4), or nitric acid (HNO3)???  (-- 
the most common types.) Phosphoric and sulfuric acid are more easily 
created from minerals found in mines. Or is a potion of acid magical and 
all this chemsitry can just be forgotton?

